  "title": "Erdős Problem #629",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "The list chromatic number $\\chi_L(G)$ is defined to be the minimal $k$ such that for any assignment of a list of $k$ colours to each vertex of $G$ (perhaps different lists for different vertices) a colouring of each vertex by a colour on its list can be chosen such that adjacent vertices receive distinct colours.\nDetermine the minimal number of vertices $n(k)$ of a bipartite graph $G$ such that $\\chi_L(G)>k$.",
